## 🔧 **Proposed Fix**

### Option A: Route Order Fix (Most Likely)
**Issue:** Agent routes mounted after protected routes in `app.ts`

**Fix:**
```typescript
// In src/app.ts - move agent routes BEFORE agentProtected section
app.route('/', healthRoutes)
app.route('/webapp/swap', swapRoutes) 
app.route('/webapp', webappRoutes)

// MOVE THIS UP - before agentProtected
app.route('/v1/agent', agentRoutes)
app.route('/a2a', a2aRoutes)

// Legacy internal API routes - X-Agent-Key required
const agentProtected = new Hono()
agentProtected.use('*', agentKeyAuth(config.agentApiKey))
// ... rest of protected routes
```

### Option B: Explicit Route Exclusion  
**Issue:** Global middleware catching all routes

**Fix:**
```typescript
// In src/app.ts - exclude registration from protected routes
const agentProtected = new Hono()
agentProtected.use('*', agentKeyAuth(config.agentApiKey))
// Exclude /v1/agent/* from this middleware group
```

### Option C: Middleware Specificity
**Issue:** Agent routes incorrectly protected

**Fix:**
```typescript
// In src/routes/agent.ts - ensure registration is not protected
agentRoutes.post('/register', /* no auth middleware */, async (c) => {
// Other agent routes with auth:  
agentRoutes.use('*', agentBearerAuth) // Apply to all other routes
agentRoutes.post('/quote', /* protected */, async (c) => {
```

